From a94e2982205d1054db7c0ee7974b311d36bd7f88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: T <t@d.local>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 23:58:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] A1, A2 and items 19-21. A1: the book arm now announces itself
 when suppressed - BOOK ARM SKIPPED with the computed reason - so a nan is
 always attributable and no-pool cannot be confused with a provenance
 mismatch, which is what concealed the key mismatch through three deliveries.
 A2: bar_day is threaded into the book arm and asserted non-None, because with
 it absent evaluate_valid falls back to exit-day groups and the arm would
 apply a V3b variant while the catalogue and the null apply the specified
 entry-basis one. Item 20 as the authorised deviation: new engine/runlog.py
 times every stage and the run itself emits the timing table with the
 genuinely concurrent fraction stated, rather than costing a separate
 profiling run. Item 21: the run log is auto-written into the output tree as
 an attestation record carrying wall-clock, console output is tee'd so
 watching, piping and redirecting all read the same, warnings go to the log
 and a Progress helper gives a progress line, heartbeat and ETA. Item 19
 scoped to the F0 re-score: 19,757 independent re-scores parallelise across
 the worker pool while deduplicate stays single-pass in ascending chunk order,
 with f0_parity_proof asserting the parallel result equals the serial one and
 aborting if not.

